   "d": "2021-10-19",
   "doc": "Q3 TU",
   "fy": "FY21",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "The recurring revenue growth rate from H1 (12% at constant currency) has been sustained in Q3, and net cash at 30 September 2021 was up £0.3m at £2.3m.",
   "file": "20211019_GETB_Trading-Update-and-Bolt-on-Acquisitions.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-01-20",
   "doc": "YE-TU",
   "fy": "FY21",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -1,
   "q": "Adjusted loss is expected to be in-line with market expectations* as the Group continues to make investments in customer acquisition and its capabilities to underpin long term growth.",
   "file": "20220120_GETB_Trading-Update,-New-Wins-and-Notice-of-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-03-01",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "RAISE",
   "s": 1,
   "q": "We have entered the new year with encouraging momentum from our high-quality recurring subscription revenues and we now anticipate 2022 revenue growth will be ahead of expectations#, enabling us to increase investment in long-term growth across our business.",
   "file": "20220301_GETB_2021-Audited-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-05-05",
   "doc": "AGM",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "The Board reaffirms its expectations* for 2022 with a very high level of confidence.",
   "file": "20220505_GETB_AGM-Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-07-13",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "RAISE",
   "s": 1,
   "q": "Group expected to remain modestly profitable at the Adjusted EBITDA level during H2 2022, marginally ahead of current expectations for 2022",
   "file": "20220713_GETB_2022-Half-year-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-12-14",
   "doc": "YE-TU",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "RAISE",
   "s": 1,
   "q": "The Board anticipates financial results for the year ended 31 December 2022 to be slightly ahead of market expectations, in line with the Group's strategic focus on growth.",
   "file": "20221214_GETB_Trading-update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-03-01",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -1,
   "q": "The strong ARR momentum from 2022 has continued into 2023, with robust January trading. We have started to scale our investments in customer acquisition, including in sales and marketing heads, in both the US and UK and we expect those investments to deliver meaningful returns over the medium-term.",
   "file": "20230301_GETB_2022-Audited-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-04-28",
   "doc": "AGM",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "The Board is pleased to reconfirm expectations* for the year with a high level of confidence.",
   "file": "20230428_GETB_AGM-Statement.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-09-05",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "The Group's underlying trading continues to be in line with market expectations****, remaining modestly profitable at the Adjusted EBITDA* level during H2 2023 as it continues to invest in long-term growth, with strong cash inflows from H2-weighted customer renewals",
   "file": "20230905_GETB_2023-Half-year-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2024-01-18",
   "doc": "YE-TU",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "RAISE",
   "s": 1,
   "q": "Adjusted Loss before Tax is expected to be slightly better than market expectations.",
   "file": "20240118_GETB_Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2024-03-26",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "2024 has started well, with continued growth across the Group through a combination of new business, expansion and price improvement.",
